    { "id": "flow-note", "x": 0, "y": -300, "w": 700, "page": "page-1", "text": "Desktop, 1440 x 900. The controls work: the step rail on the left jumps back to any screen you have answered, the counter refuses a fourth temperament, and Continue stays dead until the screen is answered.\n\nGender is now screen one. Nothing before it says she or he, and everything after it takes the answer." },
    { "id": "gap-note", "x": 780, "y": -300, "w": 660, "page": "page-1", "text": "Deliberately absent: no voice picker, no sub-picker under Games. The server collects a name, three temperaments, up to three interests, one feeling and eight appearance answers. Nothing else. A control that submits nothing is worse than no control." },
    { "id": "pronoun-note", "x": 1580, "y": 3240, "w": 700, "page": "page-2", "text": "The top row carries the point. Screen two is shown twice, once for each answer to screen one: the copy and the sample silhouette both follow it, and neither exists before the question is asked." }
